mantle rm260
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_ansel_kelpford
title the sail sampler
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=crafter
traits temper=short talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk stitches_ships_from_memory_on_one_long_scrap
likes smoked_eel swimming old_maps frosty_mornings
dislikes stale_bread bad_manners
fears a_missing_landing_rung debt_on_a_blank_page
hopes a_strip_long_enough_for_the_whole_sound a_clear_swimming_channel
topics land +0.4 work +0.3 pastimes +0.5 gossip -0.5
styles comfort=practical gossip=blunt refuse=terse tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# stitches the outlines of passing ships on a long scrap, goes quiet when the shore comes in sight, and has little patience with an elbow in the ribs.

words
oath! = Bent eye and split thread | Rot in the seam
saying! = Let the outline earn the name | Slack for a bend, tight for a spar
sampler = my rag fleet | a sail roll of my own making
mastmark = a long grey stitch | a tall red stitch
hullmark = a crooked row of blue | a dark running stitch
tack = a single pale tack | a short holding stitch
breadheel = a heel like a clog | a scuffed-looking crust
eelpiece = a thumb of smoked eel | a dark strip of eel
watermark = a bleached stripe on the stone | a greenish line along the wall
chartfold = a bald crease in the paper | a white fold worn smooth
rolltie = a double length of thread | a tie from the selvedge
mapweight = a thick button | a chipped flat bead
seamend = a knotted tail | a turned-back stitch
frostleaf = a silver leaf on the sill | a leaf stiff as tin

any
opinion dole for 2 : Give a wolf bread while there's still strength to chew it. Forms and questions can wait till the second slice.
opinion church for 1 : At the chapel I got a bowlful right down to the bottom. Some places the serving spoon just skims the broth.
opinion houses against 2 : We have to stand clear when a House boat comes in. I've been waiting to hear where the rest of us should land.
opinion festivals against 1 : Somebody always takes a nice plain ship and hangs flags everywhere till you can't see how it's made.
opinion watch against 1 : A Watch shoulder feels just as sharp as any other in a crowd, whatever's on the badge.
opinion merchants against 2 : Smoked eel gets thinner and dearer going up the street. Only thing growing on the way is the price.

grown
line greet : Give me a breath to lay my thread aside. Welcome. | There's room on my seaward side.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Frost or no frost, you're early. I like that.
line greet.return : A straight greeting. I'll answer it gladly. | Aye, I've a moment between stitches.
line again.open : Got a little further on my strip since we spoke.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : You're near enough to put your coat on mine.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Over by the rolled cloth! Here.
line farewell : Go easy by the landing steps. | Give yourself a little slack going home.
line farewell.return : You're clear of my loose thread. Go well.
line react.news : Speak so I can see the shape of what happened.
line react.news.new : That puts a different ship in the picture.
line react.news.known : I had the outline. Now it's got some colour on it.
line react.news.doubt : Who had a clear sight of it?
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=loss|death|crime|assault|theft] : I can put this roll away and walk beside you for a bit.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=work|birth|marriage] : Worth a bright stitch to remember it by.
line ask.how : How's the day wearing against you?
line answer.how : Settled. There's thread enough here to finish today's stitching.
line sympathise : A rough thing rubbed in the same place makes one mighty sore.
line reassure : You could sit on my coat till the shaking eases.
line decline : No. Please keep your paws off my roll.
line accept_decline : Fair. I leave your things in your keeping.
line thank : You left me room to do it properly. Much obliged.
line deflect_thanks : Mind the next wolf has room as well.
line preclose : My loose end's trailing. Better see to that.
line accept_preclose : I'll let you by without a fuss.
line ack : Clear as a mast against snow.

scene sampler
when topic=pastimes|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can pick a boat off #sampler# just by feeling for the spars. | I can carry half the Sound inside my cuff.
b : Even if the sails are down? | That's a curious claim for one small cuff.
a : Especially then. Sailcloth flaps about and hides the interesting bit. | Look at the stitching. There's the low one with the mast set well forward. Plenty more rolled up.

scene eel
when topic=food self.likes=smoked_eel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put #eelpiece# between slices so soft the eel leaves a mark. | I save the smoky outside for the last bite.
b : Why does the mark matter? | Stronger taste at the edge?
a : When the eel's finished, I still have the bread it touched. | Yes. The middle's all rich and mild. I want smoke to be the taste that lingers.

scene frostleaf
when topic=weather self.likes=frosty_mornings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I pick up #frostleaf# by its stalk. | Frost sets all the lines of a cobweb out plain.
b : What for? | Till something blunders through?
a : To see the shape whole before it goes limp. Back to its sill before the frost thaws. | Yes. That's the moment to look, from a little distance.

scene seamtug
when topic=work self.job=crafter self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I draw a stitch up till the cloth just begins to object. | One tight stitch can spoil a long tidy seam.
b : How can you feel that? | How would I see which one?
a : The cloth loses its give. Let half a breath out of the thread and it lies flat again. | Run the seam between your pads. The hard little ridge is your culprit.

scene rudeeye
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=bad_manners
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : I don't care for somebody reading a map over my elbow without a word. | If you need to get past me, say so before the shove.
b : Hard to read with somebody breathing on the page. | A word takes less room than an elbow.
a : Exactly. Ask and I'll hold it wide. Breathe down my neck and it goes straight in my coat. | That's my point. I'd sooner move willingly.

scene boxchart
when topic=land self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An old map puts water where I can stand dry now. | Here's #chartfold#, right through the drawn coast.
b : Is it any use if it's wrong? | Is the coast entirely rubbed out?
a : Yes. It lets me picture the ground twice over without shifting my feet. | A little bay might be lost there. A patch of mystery suits me.

scene swimpath
when topic=pastimes self.likes=swimming
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I choose where I'll get out before I choose where I'll go in. | From the water a perfectly good landing looks like one long wall.
b : Don't those places tend to be the same? | Where do you look for the steps?
a : On a calm day, perhaps. Water has business of its own. | Beside the post I picked when my eyes were still above the quay.

scene nobread
when topic=food self.dislikes=stale_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've had #breadheel# try to fight its way out of my bowl. | A loaf ought to bend a little under my thumb.
b : Did the bread win? | Even if it has a stiff crust?
a : It got a fair knock at my chin. Eventually I drowned it in broth. | Under the crust, yes. I want to eat lunch without a hammer.

scene sparline
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I save long bits of cloth, whatever colour I'm offered. | I'd exchange a square scrap for a narrower, longer piece.
b : Have you no liking for one colour? | What good is a long thin scrap?
a : For stitching, plenty. But I'm running out of water to put my ships on. | It rolls up. A square would have me folding a mast in half.

scene thinwall
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The Sump gives me a fair chance of hearing the water through a shut door. | I've got used to putting my good things on pegs.
b : Wouldn't it be quieter inland? | Higher than the floor?
a : Quiet isn't everything. I like knowing the world's still moving beyond the boards. | Higher than a wet coat swinging off somebody's shoulder.

scene coin
when topic=prices self.wealth=poor|destitute
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I count my coins I lay them out like boats waiting for a berth. | I leave enough money for thread before I think about fish.
b : Which one gets a berth first? | Wouldn't fish make a better supper?
a : The broad one for bread. The smaller ones come in if there's room. | Tonight, yes. Next week I'd have supper and no cuff left on my coat.

scene finish
when topic=work self.job=crafter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd sooner leave a little marker than lose my place in my work. | A mark in pale thread will come out clean when it's done its job.
b : What marker goes there? | Why go to that trouble?
a : A loose cross in another colour. I know where I was without guessing wrong. | Because a black thumbprint won't come out just because I'm finished with it.

scene friendroll
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I wouldn't mind #self.friend# seeing the length of this roll. | #self.friend# can hold one end if I take it outside.
b : Is the length a secret? | Does it take two wolves now?
a : No. I just don't want a row of strangers guessing what I meant by every knot. | If there's wind, yes. I'm making ships. I'd sooner the cloth didn't try to set sail.

scene figurewake
when topic=animals
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A gull's shadow makes a fine little sail on quiet water. | I'd know a swimming bird a long way off by the way the wake widens.
b : Till the gull turns? | Wouldn't a boat make the same shape?
a : Till the gull lands. Then I've got a boat with feathers that keeps trying to eat things. | Longer cut at the front. Watch the water at the bows next time.

scene quiet
when topic=day here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At dusk I stitch in one colour at a time. | Once the horizon goes I roll the ships up for the night.
b : Why change how you do it? | Can't you do another from memory?
a : Because blue and soot look alike by poor light. Nobody wants an unplanned black cloud on a fine day. | I've done a fair few that way. But it's pleasant to end the work when the last real mast goes dark.

scene repaired
when topic=home|work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I turn a worn cuff round so the good edge takes its share. | One new button makes the rest of a coat seem a little weary.
b : Does the turn show? | Would you change all the buttons then?
a : Yes. Shows I've got some more useful life out of it. | I'd use an odd one and let it be odd. The coat's still warm.

scene dreamwater
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In a dream the whole Sound lay in a basin with a smooth blue rim. | I dreamt a needle could move ships about on my sampler.
b : Did you put your paw in? | Where did you send them?
a : A little boat showed just below the surface. I was afraid of upsetting it. | Home, every last one. Which left a very dull view at sea.

scene excuses
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / challenge / assess
a : I can put a name to a ship from shore. Recognising everybody aboard is another matter. | I don't stitch a wolf on deck because I saw a patch of brown there.
b : You can't even make a guess? | Could be a coat, all the same.
a : I could make a dozen. You'd carry away the one that suited you. | Or a coil of rope. That's why I leave the deck plain.

story rollwind [topic=memories]
  : I took my strip of sewn boats up where I could see the originals.
  : A gust got under the cloth. I caught the far end with my teeth and the whole fleet filled my mouth.
  b : Were the stitches all right?
  : Perfect. My tongue tasted of cheap blue dye for a morning.

story wrongroad [topic=land self.likes=old_maps]
  : I followed a lane on an old map till I came up against a fine high wall.
  : I laid the map across my knees. The wall was younger than the road, and the map older than both my knees.
  b : How did you finish your walk?
  : Walked the length of the wall and back. I've drawn myself a thin line on the map, in pencil.

story notmycap [topic=pastimes self.likes=swimming]
  : I'd put my cap on a landing post while I swam. Coming back, I picked out the post by the shape on top.
  : It wasn't a cap. A fat gull got up and gave me its full opinion of swimmers.
  b : Where was your cap?
  : One post farther down. No opinion of me whatsoever, which suited me better.

rule @hem
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=crafter
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leave the last seam loose a moment. | That's a fold for turning, keep it flat!

rule @landing
when concept=bark self.likes=swimming
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Landing rung's wet, get a proper grip. | Don't set a bundle on the step out.

rule @map
when concept=bark self.likes=old_maps
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One thumb holds the map in this wind. | Corners down or you'll lose the coast.

rule @streets
when concept=bark here.place=market
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A word before the elbow, please. | Room enough if you ask for it.

dlg resident.hub : I'm rolling up some cloth. There's an ear free if you've business.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : You remember my fleet, #topic.player#. I've found another mast for it.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Stand there and I'll hear you. This much room suits me.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=dusk] : Nearly too dull to thread a needle. Speak while I've still light to see your face.
dlg resident.job [self.job=crafter] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. There's a place for a steady stitch and I know where to take one.
dlg resident.job : Give me the loose end and I'll see where I can help.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : Here's what came through clearly enough. #world.news#.
dlg resident.bye : May you find a sound foothold at the water.

graft resident.hub
choice Unroll a little of that fleet for me. -> narrow_fleet
node narrow_fleet
say See that short blue line with two little uprights? Look back towards the water and you'll know the shape before you can read what's on the bow.
choice How did you choose where to start? -> first_vessel
choice Let the roll close. -> hub
node first_vessel
say The boat passing when I had spare cloth and a free paw. Look how big I made it. Hadn't reckoned on giving its neighbours room.
choice Help wind the roll up. -> hub
choice Keep walking. -> bye
